    "long_instructions": "###Producing CSS\r\nUsing AI, produce a CSS file for the webpage your previously worked on. \r\n\r\n## Steps \r\n1. Add your HTML file from level 12 by clicking on the backpack icon to the left.\r\n\r\n\t(if you didn't save to the backpack - go back to level 12 to save)\r\n\t- Select import from backback\r\n    - Select the correct file using the drop down\r\n    - Click `Import to Project`\r\n    - *notice there are now two files: an HTML file and a CSS file*\r\n2. Switch to AI mode and ask the AI to enhance your dog website using CSS. Start with a simple prompt, like asking it to add a CSS file. \r\n3. Accept the code to add the `styles.css` file. \r\n4. Next, refine the design by describing the changes you want until the page looks the way you envision. Spend as much or a little time here as you like. \r\n\r\n## Debug \r\nIf you notice the CSS changes do not show up in the preview, Ask the AI to help you debug. \r\nA common error is the not linking the CSS file to the HTML.\r\n\r\n::: details [**🔎 Show me how**]\r\nThe common error here is that the `CSS` File is not linked to the `HTML` file. \r\nAdd \r\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"styles.css\">\r\nto the head section of your 'HTML' file\r\n\r\n![](https://images.code.org/03cf50f51e34a0c0abd83c1d6c4a6a21-image-1761073206253.png)\r\n(*drag the window out to enlarge the code*)\r\n:::\r\n\r\n \r\n## Need more support?\r\nWatch the video tutorial on the previous level. \r\n",
    "level_system_prompt": "This activity is designed to show student CSS structure without HTML or JavaScript. Do not produce HTML or JavaScript even if the user asks for specific styling or functionality. ",
